{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this stay. Can you tell me what brought you back to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I was just discharged yesterday, but this morning at 2 AM, I started feeling nauseous again. It happened right after I started my tube feed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And how many times did you vomit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:18:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t know, maybe around 100 times? It was mostly white phlegm. Then my whole abdomen started hurting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:19:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds really rough. Any fever, chest pain, or dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:19:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever or chest pain. But I do feel short of breath when I vomit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. We’ll monitor that. Your vitals are stable now. We’re going to give you some IV fluids and medications for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will you use the same meds as last time? Morphine and Ativan helped the most."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with IV Zofran, Ativan, Compazine, and a little morphine. That’s what worked before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-04-07 17:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just don’t understand why this keeps happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-04-07 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back. Potassium was low at 3.6, and your bicarbonate was 21, which suggests mild metabolic acidosis. We think it’s from dehydration due to vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-04-07 18:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I had low potassium last time too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-04-07 18:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s manageable. We’re giving you potassium and fluids through the IV. It should correct over the next day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-04-07 18:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-04-08 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-04-08 09:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. No nausea or pain. My stomach still feels a little sensitive, but I’m not vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-04-08 09:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your repeat labs show your potassium went up to 6.4 earlier, so we paused the supplement, and now it’s back to 3.9. We’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-04-08 09:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, it went too high? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-04-08 09:14:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. It’s common when correcting levels. We adjusted the dose, and it’s back in a safe range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-04-08 09:15:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-04-08 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The gastroenterology team reviewed your case. You’ve had a lot of testing—gastric emptying, manometry, nerve studies—all showing severe motility issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-04-08 10:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and nothing’s helped much. I’ve tried so many meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-04-08 10:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. They said we’ve reached the limit of what we can do medically. The best approach now is to stick with your tube feeds and small sips if you feel up to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-04-08 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s just about managing symptoms now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-04-08 10:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. They recommend continuing your current meds as needed and following up with your specialist, Dr. ___ at ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-04-08 10:36:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see. I was hoping there was something new, but I guess I’ll keep doing what works."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-04-08 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to restart your tube feeds at 90 mL/hr. That’s your usual rate, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-04-08 14:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s correct. Should I be worried it might trigger another episode?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-04-08 14:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go slow and watch you closely. The team thinks the previous flare may have been from increasing the rate too fast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-04-08 14:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, that makes sense. I did try to speed it up a little yesterday morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-04-08 14:24:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could definitely be the trigger. Stick to the prescribed rate, and you should do better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-04-09 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your labs this morning look stable. Bicarbonate is now 22, so your acidosis has resolved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-04-09 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. And I’ve had no nausea since yesterday. The tube feed is going smoothly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-04-09 08:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Your thyroid levels are stable too, so we’ll keep you on your usual levothyroxine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-04-09 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad everything’s back on track. When do you think I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-04-09 08:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you keep doing this well, probably tomorrow morning. We’ll write up your discharge orders today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-04-09 08:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure my husband knows."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-04-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re ready to go home. Continue your tube feeds at 90 mL/hr, take your meds as prescribed, and follow up with your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-04-10 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start feeling nauseous again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-04-10 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use your PRN meds—Zofran, Ativan, or Dronabinol. If it doesn’t improve, or if you can’t keep fluids down, come back to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-04-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-04-10 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-04-07 17:09:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-04-10 11:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of gastroparesis, J-tube placement, and Nissen fundoplication was readmitted less than 24 hours after discharge due to recurrent nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain. Symptoms began after increasing her tube feed rate and were consistent with her usual gastroparesis flares. She received IV antiemetics, morphine, and fluids, with resolution of symptoms by the next day. Metabolic acidosis from dehydration improved with treatment, and electrolytes stabilized. She tolerated tube feeds at 90 mL/hr without further vomiting. The gastroenterology team concluded that diagnostic and therapeutic options are exhausted and recommended ongoing symptom management with tube feeds and PRN medications. She was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up arranged.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Acidosis",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Unspecified vitamin D deficiency",
      "Osteoporosis, unspecified",
      "Other postprocedural status",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of other sites",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast"
    ]
  }
}
